net: openvswitch: conntrack: remove 'add_helper' dead code

jira KERNEL-1962
cve CVE-2026-98490
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-741.27.1.el9_9
commit-author Ilya Maximets <i.maximets@ovn.org>
commit 5e6c14dd42a1c1fe938e573dc6c9098145b2b0c4
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-741.27.1.el9_9/5e6c14dd.failed

This variable can only become 'true' when the connection is not
confirmed, but it is only checked when it is confirmed.  So, it can be
treated as being always false and just removed.

Fixes: 3c1860543fcc ("openvswitch: add nf_ct_is_confirmed check before assigning the helper")
	Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
	Signed-off-by: Ilya Maximets <i.maximets@ovn.org>
	Reviewed-by: Aaron Conole <aconole@redhat.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260921145655.3167436-3-i.maximets@ovn.org
	Signed-off-by: Jakub Kicinski <kuba@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit 5e6c14dd42a1c1fe938e573dc6c9098145b2b0c4)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

